+# TLS backend
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Rustls as the TLS backend, chosen because it is a good fit for a Rust codebase, has fewer CVEs, and is simpler. Certificate verification is required on all builds, with self-signed certificates used for testing instead of disabling verification, and all internal services must use HTTPS with no plaintext HTTP exceptions.
